## COST ESTIMATION FORMULAS

### Formula Components:
```
Total Cost = Compute + Database + Storage + Network + Third-Party + Overhead

Compute = (Base Infrastructure) + (Per-Request Cost × Request Volume)
Database = (Instance Cost) + (Storage Cost × Data Volume) + (IOPS Cost)
Storage = (Object Storage × Data Volume) + (Backup Cost)
Network = (Data Transfer Out × Transfer Volume) + (CDN Cost)
Third-Party = (Auth Services) + (Payment Gateway) + (Monitoring) + (APIs)
Overhead = (DevOps Salaries) + (Support Tools) + (Compliance Audits)
```

### Scaling Coefficients:
```
Year 1 (10K users):   Coefficient = 1.0x    (Baseline)
Year 3 (100K users):  Coefficient = 8-12x   (Economies of scale kick in)
Year 5 (1M users):    Coefficient = 60-100x (Bulk pricing, reserved instances)
Year 10 (10M users):  Coefficient = 400-800x (Enterprise agreements, custom pricing)
```

### Per-User Economics:
```
Year 1:  $1.50-5.00 per user/month (high overhead, small scale)
