| Bottleneck | Mitigation | When to Implement | Estimated Cost Impact |
|------------|-----------|-------------------|----------------------|
| Database reads | Read replicas (3+), Redis caching | Year 1 (10K users) | +30% DB cost |
| Database writes | Sharding (by user_id), CQRS pattern | Year 3 (100K users) | +100% DB cost, -50% latency |
| API throughput | Horizontal scaling (HPA), load balancing | Year 1 (10K users) | +50% compute cost |
| Global latency | Multi-region deployment, edge caching | Year 2 (50K users) | +200% infra cost |
| Data volume | Archiving (S3 Glacier), cold storage | Year 2 (50K users) | -70% storage cost |
| Search performance | Elasticsearch with sharding | Year 2 (50K users) | +$1K-5K/month |
| Real-time updates | WebSockets with Redis pub/sub | Year 1 (10K users) | +$500-2K/month |
| Background jobs | Kafka + worker pools (auto-scaling) | Year 1 (10K users) | +30% compute cost |
| Static assets | Multi-CDN (CloudFront + Cloudflare) | Year 1 (10K users) | +$500-2K/month |
| Database connections | Connection pooling (PgBouncer, ProxySQL) | Year 1 (10K users) | +$100-300/month |

## Failure Modes & Resilience
| Failure | Detection | Mitigation | Fallback | RTO | RPO |
|---------|-----------|------------|----------|-----|-----|
| Database primary down | Health checks (5s interval) | Automatic failover to replica | Read-only mode for 30s | 30s | 0s (synchronous replication) |
| External API down (Stripe) | Circuit breaker (3 failures → open) | Queue for retry (exponential backoff) | "Payment pending" message | N/A | 0s (queued) |
| Cache stampede (Redis) | Cache warming, distributed locks | Staggered TTLs, single-flight requests | Direct database (degraded performance) | 0s | N/A |
| DDoS attack | Traffic anomaly detection (ML) | Rate limiting + WAF + challenge page | Graceful degradation (static content) | 60s | N/A |
| Region failure (AWS us-east-1) | Route 53 health checks (30s interval) | Automatic DNS failover to us-west-2 | Full service in alternate region | 2-5m | 5m (async replication) |
| Kafka partition unavailable | Consumer group rebalancing | Automatic reassignment to healthy partitions | Temporary message queue (SQS) | 30s | 0s (replicated) |
| Certificate expiration | Certificate monitoring (14 days notice) | Automatic renewal (Let's Encrypt, ACM) | Manual renewal, zero downtime | N/A | N/A |
| Disk full (database) | CloudWatch alarm (90% threshold) | Automatic storage expansion (AWS RDS) | Manual intervention, read-only mode | 5m | 0s |

## Disaster Recovery & Business Continuity

### Backup Strategy
- **Database**: 
  - Automated daily snapshots (retained 30 days)
  - Point-in-time recovery (PITR) for last 7 days
  - Cross-region backup replication (async, 15-minute lag)
- **Object Storage**: 
  - Versioning enabled (retain last 10 versions)
  - Cross-region replication (S3 CRR, GCS multi-region)
  - Lifecycle policies (archive after 90 days, delete after 7 years)
- **Configuration**: 
  - Infrastructure-as-code (Terraform state in S3 with versioning)
  - Secrets backed up to encrypted S3 bucket (cross-region)
  - Application config in Git (immutable, versioned)

### Recovery Procedures
1. **Database Failure**: Promote read replica to primary (30s RTO)
2. **Region Failure**: Failover to DR region via DNS (2-5m RTO)
3. **Data Corruption**: Restore from snapshot + replay WAL logs (15-30m RTO)
4. **Ransomware Attack**: Restore from immutable backups in isolated account (1-4h RTO)

### Testing Schedule
- **Tabletop Exercises**: Quarterly (disaster scenarios, decision-making)
- **Failover Drills**: Monthly (automated, non-production)
- **Full DR Test**: Semi-annually (production failover, measure RTO/RPO)

